#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-sessions: keep track of your local Claude Code sessions.

A terminal list and a live dashboard (http://localhost:7799) for every Claude
Code session on this machine: which are open, which need you, which have a PR
waiting for review, and which are done. Python 3.8+ standard library only;
`gh` (GitHub CLI) is used for PR states when installed.

    cc-sessions                 sessions grouped by what they need
    cc-sessions -a              include done and old sessions
    cc-sessions show ID         details: PRs, links, files, last message
    cc-sessions done ID [NOTE]  mark solved          (undone ID to reopen)
    cc-sessions park ID         set aside for later   (unpark ID)
    cc-sessions note ID TEXT    attach your own note
    cc-sessions resume ID       cd to the session's folder and `claude --resume`
    cc-sessions serve           run the dashboard in the foreground
    cc-sessions open            open the dashboard in the browser
    cc-sessions install         hooks + background service + app launcher
    cc-sessions uninstall       remove all of that again

ID is a row number from the last list or any unique prefix of a session id.
"""

